    "# <span style=\"color:red\"> Lecture 13: Silent Errors, Testing, and Debugging </span>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<font size=\"4\">\n",
    "\n",
    "In the previous class we:\n",
    "- Sorted our mistakes into **syntax errors**, **runtime errors**, and **silent errors**\n",
    "- Learned to read a **traceback** from the bottom up\n",
    "- Kept our code alive with **`try`** and **`except`** - and saw how `except: pass` manufactures silent errors\n",
    "- Asked the user a question with **`input()`**, and learned that it always hands back a string"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<font size=\"4\">\n",
    "\n",
    "In this class we will:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Meet the third kind of mistake head-on: code that runs perfectly and **lies to you**\n",
    "- Use a **plot** to catch a bug that the printed output was hiding\n",
    "- Make our code check itself with **`assert`**\n",
    "- Write **tests**: small cases where we already know the right answer\n",
    "- Put it all together into a repeatable **debugging recipe**"
   ]
  },
